The note points to the **VFSUB** instruction family (vector floating-point subtraction).

## RVV Instructions

| Instruction | Assembly Format | Description |
|-------------|-----------------|-------------|
| vfsub.vv | `vfsub.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm` | Vector-vector: vd[i] = vs2[i] - vs1[i] |
| vfsub.vf | `vfsub.vf vd, vs2, rs1, vm` | Vector-scalar: vd[i] = vs2[i] - f[rs1] |
| vfrsub.vf | `vfrsub.vf vd, vs2, rs1, vm` | Reverse vector-scalar: vd[i] = f[rs1] - vs2[i] |

**Operands:**
- `vd`: destination vector register (floating-point)
- `vs2`: first source vector register (floating-point)
- `vs1`: second source vector register (floating-point) for .vv form
- `rs1`: scalar floating-point register for .vf forms
- `vm`: optional vector mask (v0.t or omitted)

**Behavior:** Single-width floating-point subtraction with IEEE 754-2008 rounding and exception semantics. Uses the dynamic rounding mode in `frm`. Supports all standard FP exceptions (invalid, overflow, underflow, inexact, divide-by-zero).

## C Intrinsics

```c
