// Vector-scalar
vfloat32m1_t __riscv_vfsub_vf_f32m1(vfloat32m1_t vs2, float32_t rs1, size_t vl);
vfloat64m1_t __riscv_vfsub_vf_f64m1(vfloat64m1_t vs2, float64_t rs1, size_t vl);

// Reverse vector-scalar
vfloat32m1_t __riscv_vfrsub_vf_f32m1(vfloat32m1_t vs2, float32_t rs1, size_t vl);
vfloat64m1_t __riscv_vfrsub_vf_f64m1(vfloat64m1_t vs2, float64_t rs1, size_t vl);
```

Masked variants (`_m` suffix) and all LMUL configurations (m1, m2, m4, m8, mf2, mf4, mf8) follow standard naming.

The note describes the **saturating add** instruction family (`vsadd`/`vsaddu`).

**RVV Instructions:**

| Instruction | Assembly Format | Description |
|-------------|-----------------|-------------|
| `vsadd.vv` | `vsadd.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm` | Signed saturating add, vector-vector |
| `vsadd.vx` | `vsadd.vx vd, vs2, rs1, vm` | Signed saturating add, vector-scalar |
| `vsaddu.vv` | `vsaddu.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm` | Unsigned saturating add, vector-vector |
| `vsaddu.vx` | `vsaddu.vx vd, vs2, rs1, vm` | Unsigned saturating add, vector-scalar |

**Operands:** `vd` (destination vector), `vs2` (first source vector), `vs1`/`rs1` (second source: vector or scalar `x` register), `vm` (optional mask).

**Saturation behavior:** Results saturate at the minimum/maximum representable value for the element width; no `vxrm` rounding mode applies (saturating adds are exact). The `vxsat` CSR bit is set to 1 if any element saturated.

