vint8mf4_t __riscv_vcompress_vm_i8mf4(vint8mf4_t vs2, vbool32_t mask, size_t vl);
vint8mf2_t __riscv_vcompress_vm_i8mf2(vint8mf2_t vs2, vbool16_t mask, size_t vl);
vint8m1_t  __riscv_vcompress_vm_i8m1 (vint8m1_t  vs2, vbool8_t  mask, size_t vl);
vint8m2_t  __riscv_vcompress_vm_i8m2 (vint8m2_t  vs2, vbool4_t  mask, size_t vl);
vint8m4_t  __riscv_vcompress_vm_i8m4 (vint8m4_t  vs2, vbool2_t  mask, size_t vl);
vint8m8_t  __riscv_vcompress_vm_i8m8 (vint8m8_t  vs2, vbool1_t  mask, size_t vl);
// ... and for uint16/32/64, float16/32/64 with corresponding type suffixes
```

Note: This is **mask-selection** (not index-selection; `viota`+`vrgather` would handle index-based gather). The mask is always `v0` in the base encoding; intrinsics expose it explicitly.

The described behavior maps to the **vmerge** instruction family (vector merge).

**RVV Instructions:**

| Instruction | Assembly Format | Description |
|-------------|-----------------|-------------|
| `vmerge.vvm` | `vmerge.vvm vd, vs2, vs1, v0` | Vector-vector merge: `v0[i].LSB ? vs1[i] : vs2[i]` |
| `vmerge.vxm` | `vmerge.vxm vd, vs2, rs1, v0` | Vector-scalar merge (X-reg): `v0[i].LSB ? x[rs1] : vs2[i]` |
| `vmerge.vim` | `vmerge.vim vd, vs2, imm, v0` | Vector-immediate merge: `v0[i].LSB ? imm : vs2[i]` |

**Operand roles:** `vd` = destination, `vs2` = unselected value (pass-through), `vs1`/`rs1`/`imm` = selected value when mask bit set, `v0` = mask register (LSB selects; unmasked elements take `vs2`).

**RVV C Intrinsics:**

```c
// Vector-vector merge
vint8m1_t __riscv_vmerge_vvm_i8m1(vint8m1_t vs2, vint8m1_t vs1, vbool8_t mask, size_t vl);
vfloat32m2_t __riscv_vmerge_vvm_f32m2(vfloat32m2_t vs2, vfloat32m2_t vs1, vbool16_t mask, size_t vl);

// Vector-scalar merge (X-reg)
vint32m1_t __riscv_vmerge_vxm_i32m1(vint32m1_t vs2, int32_t rs1, vbool32_t mask, size_t vl);

// Vector-immediate merge
vuint64m4_t __riscv_vmerge_vim_u64m4(vuint64m4_t vs2, uint64_t imm, vbool16_t mask, size_t vl);
```

**Key distinction:** `vmerge` is **selection** (conditional choice between two operands) versus `vmv*` which is unconditional copy/broadcast. The mask `v0` is **essential** to `vmerge` operation—there is no unmasked form. Scalar operands are sign/zero-extended to SEW.

The instruction family is **vector saturating subtract** (`vssub`).

**RVV Instructions:**

| Signedness | Instruction | Assembly Format |
|------------|-------------|-----------------|
| Signed | `vssub.vv` | `vssub.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm` |
| Signed | `vssub.vx` | `vssub.vx vd, vs2, rs1, vm` |
| Unsigned | `vssubu.vv` | `vssubu.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm` |
| Unsigned | `vssubu.vx` | `vssubu.vx vd, vs2, rs1, vm` |

**Operands:** `vd` = destination vector, `vs2` = minuend vector, `vs1`/`rs1` = subtrahend (vector/scalar), `vm` = optional mask (`v0.t` or omitted).

**Semantics:** Saturating subtraction: results clamp to `[0, 2^SEW-1]` (unsigned) or `[-2^(SEW-1), 2^(SEW-1)-1]` (signed). No rounding; `vxrm` is irrelevant. `vxsat` is set to 1 if any element saturates.

