vint32m1_t __riscv_vsmul_vx_i32m1(vint32m1_t vs2, int32_t rs1, size_t vl);
vint64m1_t __riscv_vsmul_vx_i64m1(vint64m1_t vs2, int64_t rs1, size_t vl);
```

(Replace `m1` with `m2/m4/m8/mf2/mf4/mf8` and add `__riscv_vsmul_vv_i8m1_m`/`__riscv_vsmul_vx_i8m1_m` forms for masked variants.)

The clue points to the **vaverage** family, which performs averaging (logical right shift with rounding). The relevant instructions are `vaaddu.vv`, `vaaddu.vx`, `vaadd.vv`, `vaadd.vx` (signed and unsigned averaging add) and `vasubu.vv`, `vasubu.vx`, `vasub.vv`, `vasub.vx` (signed and unsigned averaging subtract).

Assembly formats:
```
vaaddu.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm   # vd[i] = round((vs2[i] + vs1[i]) >> 1)
vaaddu.vx vd, vs2, rs1, vm   # vd[i] = round((vs2[i] + x[rs1]) >> 1)
vaadd.vv  vd, vs2, vs1, vm   # signed version
vaadd.vx  vd, vs2, rs1, vm   # signed version
vasubu.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm   # vd[i] = round((vs2[i] - vs1[i]) >> 1)
vasubu.vx vd, vs2, rs1, vm   # vd[i] = round((vs2[i] - x[rs1]) >> 1)
vasub.vv  vd, vs2, vs1, vm   # signed version
vasub.vx  vd, vs2, rs1, vm   # signed version
```

Key semantic constraint: Rounding is to nearest, ties to even (round-to-nearest-up for unsigned, same rule for signed). The shift is always by 1 (fixed-point 0.5 rounding).

