__riscv_vasubu_vx_u32m1(vuint32m1_t vs2, uint32_t rs1, size_t vl);
__riscv_vasub_vv_i32m1(vint32m1_t vs2, vint32m1_t vs1, size_t vl);
__riscv_vasub_vx_i32m1(vint32m1_t vs2, int32_t rs1, size_t vl);
```

Masked variants append `_m` (e.g., `__riscv_vaaddu_vv_u32m1_m`).

The clue points to the **vfdiv** family (vector floating-point divide).

**RVV Instructions:**

| Instruction | Assembly Format | Description |
|-------------|-----------------|-------------|
| vfdiv.vv | `vfdiv.vv vd, vs2, vs1, vm` | vd[i] = vs2[i] / vs1[i] (vector ÷ vector) |
| vfdiv.vf | `vfdiv.vf vd, vs2, rs1, vm` | vd[i] = vs2[i] / rs1 (vector ÷ scalar) |
| vfrdiv.vf | `vfrdiv.vf vd, vs2, rs1, vm` | vd[i] = rs1 / vs2[i] (scalar ÷ vector, reverse) |

**Operand roles:** `vd` = destination vector, `vs2` = first source vector (dividend), `vs1`/`rs1` = divisor (vector/scalar), `vm` = vector mask (v0.t or omitted).

**Behavior:** Single-width FP division per IEEE 754-2008 with configurable rounding mode in `frm`. Raises FP exceptions (invalid, divide-by-zero, overflow, underflow, inexact) recorded in `fflags`. No estimate—exact rounded result.

