vfloat64m1_t __riscv_vfdiv_vf_f64m1(vfloat64m1_t vs2, float64_t rs1, size_t vl);

// Reverse vector-scalar: vd = rs1 / vs2
vfloat32m1_t __riscv_vfrdiv_vf_f32m1(vfloat32m1_t vs2, float32_t rs1, size_t vl);
vfloat64m1_t __riscv_vfrdiv_vf_f64m1(vfloat64m1_t vs2, float64_t rs1, size_t vl);
```

(Replace `m1` with `mf2`, `m1`, `m2`, `m4`, `m8`, `m16` and `f32`/`f64` with appropriate types for other LMUL/SEW combinations.)

The description matches the **VFNMADD/VFNMSUB** family (fused multiply-add with negation, overwriting the first multiplicand) and its related **VFMSUB/VFMADD** variants.

**VF[N]MADD/VF[N]MSUB** (single-width, overwrite first multiplicand `vs2`):

| Instruction | Operation | Assembly Format |
|-------------|-----------|-----------------|
| `vfmadd.vv` | `vd[i] = +(vs1[i] * vd[i]) + vs2[i]` | `vfmadd.vv vd, vs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfmadd.vf` | `vd[i] = +(rs1 * vd[i]) + vs2[i]` | `vfmadd.vf vd, rs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfnmadd.vv` | `vd[i] = -(vs1[i] * vd[i]) - vs2[i]` | `vfnmadd.vv vd, vs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfnmadd.vf` | `vd[i] = -(rs1 * vd[i]) - vs2[i]` | `vfnmadd.vf vd, rs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfmsub.vv` | `vd[i] = +(vs1[i] * vd[i]) - vs2[i]` | `vfmsub.vv vd, vs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfmsub.vf` | `vd[i] = +(rs1 * vd[i]) - vs2[i]` | `vfmsub.vf vd, rs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfnmsub.vv` | `vd[i] = -(vs1[i] * vd[i]) + vs2[i]` | `vfnmsub.vv vd, vs1, vs2, vm` |
| `vfnmsub.vf` | `vd[i] = -(rs1 * vd[i]) + vs2[i]` | `vfnmsub.vf vd, rs1, vs2, vm` |

Operand roles: `vd` = accumulator (also destination), `vs1`/`rs1` = second multiplicand, `vs2` = first multiplicand (overwritten addend/subtrahend).

**C intrinsics** (examples for SEW=32, LMUL=1; pattern extends to other types):

```c
